    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chapter 2 · Session 5</span>\n<h2>Session 5 — Chapter 2: Interest Rate Determination (cont')</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14260 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chương 2 · Buổi 5</span>\n<h2>Buổi 5 — Chapter 2: Interest Rate Determination (cont')</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14260 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T,U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T,U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 2: Interest Rate Determination (cont')<br>2.3. Forecasting interest rates<br><br>[Practice: 1 period(s)]<br>Point/ counter-point: Does a Large Fiscal Budget Deficit Result in Higher Interest Rate?</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Book, Slides</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>- Prepare solutions to assigned questions prior to class.<br>- Present and justify answers using appropriate concepts, frameworks, or evidence.<br>- Engage in critical discussion by evaluating peer responses and refining their own reasoning.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Group 1 - Discussion chapter 7</strong> — 1. Interpret the following statements made by Wall Street analysts and portfolio managers: “The values of some stocks are dependent on the bond market. When investors are not interested in junk bonds, the values of stocks ripe for leveraged buyouts decline.”<br><br>2. Treasury Bond An inflation-indexed Treasury bond has a par value of USD1,000 and a coupon rate of 6 percent. An investor purchases this bond and holds it for one year. During the year, the consumer price index increases by 1 percent every six months. What are the total interest payments that the investor will receive during the year?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 2 - Discussion chapter 7</strong> — 1. Interpret the following statements made by Wall Street analysts and portfolio managers: &quot;The recent practice in which firms use debt to repurchase some of their stock is a good strategy as long as the firms can withstand the stagnant economy.”<br><br>2. Inflation-Indexed Treasury Bond Assume that the U.S. economy experienced deflation during the year and that the consumer price index decreased by 1 percent in the first six months of the year and by 2 percent during the second six months of the year. If an investor had purchased inflation-indexed Treasury bonds with a par value of USD10,000 and a coupon rate of 5 percent, how much would she have received in interest during the year?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 3 - Discussion chapter 7</strong> — 1.Interpret the following statements made by Wall Street analysts and portfolio managers: &quot;Although yields among bonds are related, today’s rumors of a tax cut caused an increase in the yield on municipal bonds, while the yield on corporate bonds declined.”<br><br>2.Treasury Bond An inflation-indexed Treasury bond has a par value of USD1,000 and a coupon rate of 6 percent. An investor purchases this bond and holds it for one year. During the year, the consumer price index increases by 1 percent every six months. What are the total interest payments that the investor will receive during the year?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
