    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chapter 3 · Session 6</span>\n<h2>Session 6 — Chapter 3: Interest Rate Structure</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14260 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chương 3 · Buổi 6</span>\n<h2>Buổi 6 — Chapter 3: Interest Rate Structure</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14260 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO2</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 3: Interest Rate Structure<br>3.1. Why debt security yields vary<br>3.2. Modeling the Yield to be Offered on a Debt Security</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Book, Slides</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>- Complete assigned readings in advance and prepare key questions or reflections.<br>- Actively participate in discussions by presenting reasoned arguments, responding to peers, and engaging in constructive debate.<br>- Take structured notes and identify areas requiring further clarification or deeper analysis.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Group 1 - Discussion chapter 10</strong> — 1. What is the danger of issuing too much stock? What is the role of the securities firm that serves as the underwriter, and how can it ensure that the firm does not issue too much stock?<br><br>2. Describe a lockup provision and explain why it might be required by the lead underwriter.</li>\n<li><strong>Group 2 - Discussion Chapter 10</strong> — 1. Why do firms engage in IPOs? What is the amount of the fees that the lead underwriter and its syndicate charge a firm that is going public? Why are there many IPOs in some periods and few IPOs in other periods?<br><br>2. What does it mean to “flip” shares? Why would investors want to flip shares?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 3 - Discussion chapter 10</strong> — 1. Explain the difference between obtaining funds from a venture capital firm and engaging in an IPO. Explain how the IPO may serve as a means by which the venture capital firm can cash out.<br><br>2. Discuss the concept of asymmetric information. Explain why it may motivate firms to repurchase some of their stock.</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
