    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chapter 3 · Session 9 · assessment / review</span>\n<h2>Session 9 — Group Assignment Guidelines</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14260 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chương 3 · Buổi 9 · kiểm tra / ôn tập</span>\n<h2>Buổi 9 — Group Assignment Guidelines</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14260 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO6, CLO7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO6, CLO7</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">U</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Group Assignment Guidelines</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>- Review the project objectives, scope, deliverables, timeline, and assessment criteria.<br>- Form groups (if not pre-assigned) and establish preliminary roles, communication channels, and a working plan.<br>- Seek clarification on expectations, methodology, data requirements, and academic integrity policies (including AI use, if applicable).</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Group 1 - Exercises chapter 6-7</strong> — **1. Effective Yield**<br><br>A U.S. investor obtains British pounds when the pound is worth USD1.50 and invests in a one-year money market security that provides a yield of 5 percent (in pounds). At the end of one year, the investor converts the proceeds from the investment back to dollars at the prevailing spot rate of USD1.52 per pound. Calculate the effective yield.<br><br>**2. Return on NCDs**<br><br>Phil purchased an NCD a year ago in the secondary market for USD980,000. The NCD matures today at a price of USD1 million, and Phil received USD45,000 in interest. What is Phil’s return on the NCD?<br><br>**3. Inflation-Indexed**<br><br>Treasury Bond An inflation-indexed Treasury bond has a par value of USD1,000 and a coupon rate of 6 percent. An investor purchases this bond and holds it for one year. During the year, the consumer price index increases by 1 percent every six months. What are the total interest payments that the investor will receive during the year?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 2 - Exercises chapter 6-7</strong> — **1. T-Bill Discount**<br><br>Newly issued three-month T-bills with a par value of USD10,000 sold for USD9,700. Compute the T-bill discount.<br><br>**2. Required Rate of Return**<br><br>A money market security that has a par value of USD10,000 sells for USD8,816.60. Given that the security has a maturity of two years, what is the investor’s required rate of return?<br><br>**3. Inflation-Indexed**<br><br>Treasury Bond Assume that the U.S. economy experienced deflation during the year and that the consumer price index decreased by 1 percent in the first six months of the year and by 2 percent during the second six months of the year. If an investor had purchased inflation-indexed Treasury bonds with a par value of USD10,000 and a coupon rate of 5 percent, how much would she have received in interest during the year?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 3 - Exercises chapter 6-7</strong> — **1. Commercial Paper Yield**<br><br>Assume an investor purchased six-month commercial paper with a face value of USD1 million for USD940,000. What is the yield?<br><br>**2. T-Bill Yield**<br><br>The Treasury is selling 91-day T-bills with a face value of USD10,000 for USD9,900. If the investor holds them until maturity, calculate the yield.<br><br>**3. Inflation-Indexed**<br><br>Treasury Bond An inflation-indexed Treasury bond has a par value of USD1,000 and a coupon rate of 6 percent. An investor purchases this bond and holds it for one year. During the year, the consumer price index increases by 1 percent every six months. What are the total interest payments that the investor will receive during the year?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
