    "content": "<div class=\"ml-en\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chapter 4 · Session 13</span>\n<h2>Session 13 — Chapter 6: Money Markets (cont')</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Source: FLM syllabus 14260 · session plan</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><span class=\"eyebrow\">FIN301 · Chương 4 · Buổi 13</span>\n<h2>Buổi 13 — Chapter 6: Money Markets (cont')</h2>\n<p class=\"nhan\">Nguồn: syllabus FLM 14260 · kế hoạch buổi</p></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Type</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slides in this lesson</span><span class=\"v\">none from FLM</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"kv-grid\">\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Hình thức</span><span class=\"v\">Offline</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">LO</span><span class=\"v\">CLO3</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">ITU</span><span class=\"v\">T</span></div>\n  <div class=\"kv\"><span class=\"k\">Slide trong bài</span><span class=\"v\">FLM không có</span></div>\n</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>What this session covers (FLM, verbatim)</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nội dung buổi học (FLM, nguyên văn)</h3></div>\n<p>Chapter 6: Money Markets (cont')<br><br>[Practice: 1 period(s)]<br>Point/ counter-point: Should Firms Invest in Money Market Securities?</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Materials to read</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Tài liệu cần đọc</h3></div>\n<p>Book, Slides</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Student's tasks</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Nhiệm vụ sinh viên</h3></div>\n<p>- Prepare solutions to assigned questions prior to class.<br>- Present and justify answers using appropriate concepts, frameworks, or evidence.<br>- Engage in critical discussion by evaluating peer responses and refining their own reasoning.</p>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><h3>Constructive questions — answer them yourself first</h3></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><h3>Câu hỏi kiến tạo — tự trả lời trước</h3></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Group 2 - Discussion and Exercise chapter 14</strong> — **1. Interpret the following comment**:<br><br>“We prefer to use covered call writing to hedge our stock portfolios.”<br><br>**2. Put Options on Futures**<br><br>Purdue Savings and Loan Association purchased a put option on Treasury bond futures with a September delivery date and an exercise price of 91-16. The put option has a premium of 1-32. Assume that the price of the Treasury bond futures decreases to 88-16. Should Purdue exercise the option or should it let the option expire? What is Purdue’s net gain or loss after accounting for the premium paid on the option?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 1 - Discussion and Exercise chapter 14</strong> — **1. Interpret the following comment**:<br><br>“Our firm took a hit because we wrote put options on stocks just before the stock market crash.”<br><br>**2. Call Options on Futures**<br><br>Wisconsin, Inc., purchased a call option on Treasury bond futures at a premium of 2-00. The exercise price is 92-08. If the price of the Treasury bond futures rises to 93-08, should Wisconsin exercise the call option or should it let the option expire? What is Wisconsin’s net gain or loss after accounting for the premium paid on the option?</li>\n<li><strong>Group 3 - Discussion and Exercise chapter 14</strong> — **1. Interpret the following comment** :<br><br>“Before hedging our stock portfolio with options on index futures, we search for the index that is most appropriate.”<br><br>**2. Call Options on Futures**<br><br>DePaul Insurance Company purchased a call option on a stock index futures contract. The option premium is quoted as USD6. The exercise price is 1,430. Assume the index on the futures contract reaches 1,440. Should DePaul exercise the call option or should it let the option expire? What is the net gain or loss to DePaul after accounting for the premium paid for the option (assume the value is measured as $250 times the index)?</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"ml-en\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Detailed lecture and 🎬 video for this session: coming later. For now follow the slides, the materials and the tasks above.</div></div>\n<div class=\"ml-vi\"><div class=\"note-ct\">📝 Bài giảng chi tiết và 🎬 video cho buổi này: sẽ bổ sung sau. Trước mắt học theo slide, tài liệu và nhiệm vụ ở trên.</div></div>"
